{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "tool_calls", "index": 0, "message": {"content": "Excellent! The behavior is now consistent:
1. In lenient mode, `value(double)` produces the same output as `value(Number)` for NaN/Infinity values.
2. The written values round-trip correctly through `JsonReader` in lenient mode.
3. In strict mode, both methods throw `IllegalArgumentException` consistently.

Let me also verify the behavior is consistent between `value(double)` and `value(Number)` in terms of when the exception is thrown relative to `writeDeferredName()`. 

Looking at the original `value(Number)`:
```java
writeDeferredName();  // called first
String string = value.toString();
if (!lenient && (...)) {
  throw ...;
}
```

And original `value(double)`:
```java
if (Double.isNaN(value) || Double.isInfinite(value)) {  // check first
  throw ...;
}
writeDeferredName();  // called after
```

So there was an inconsistency: in `value(Number)`, the deferred name was written *before* the check (so on failure, the name is already consumed), while in `value(double)`, the check happened *before* writing the deferred name.

I've now made `value(double)` call `writeDeferredName()` first, then check, matching `value(Number)`'s behavior. This is the most consistent approach. Let me verify this matches the test expectations - the test `testNonFiniteDoubles` just checks that the exception is thrown, which still works.

Let me double-check the consistency with the boxed version test - in `testNonFiniteBoxedDoubles`, after a failed `value(new Double(NaN))`, the writer state has the deferred name consumed (well, there's no name here, just an array). Let me verify both behave the same now in terms of state after exception.", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": [{"function": {"arguments": "{"command":"cd /testbed && cat > /tmp/repro/Repro3.java << 'EOF'\nimport com.google.gson.stream.JsonWriter;\nimport java.io.StringWriter;\nimport java.io.IOException;\n\npublic class Repro3 {\n  public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n    // After a failed value(double) in strict mode, can we continue writing?\n    // Compare with value(Number)\n    StringWriter sw = new StringWriter();\n    JsonWriter w = new JsonWriter(sw);\n    w.beginArray();\n    try { w.value(Double.NaN); } catch (IllegalArgumentException e) {}\n    // Now try to write a valid value\n    w.value(1.0);\n    w.endArray();\n    w.close();\n    System.out.println(\"double after failure: \" + sw.toString());\n\n    StringWriter sw2 = new StringWriter();\n    JsonWriter w2 = new JsonWriter(sw2);\n    w2.beginArray();\n    try { w2.value((Number) Double.valueOf(Double.NaN)); } catch (IllegalArgumentException e) {}\n    w2.value(1.0);\n    w2.endArray();\n    w2.close();\n    System.out.println(\"Number after failure: \" + sw2.toString());\n  }\n}\nEOF\njavac -cp /tmp/gson_classes -d /tmp/repro /tmp/repro/Repro3.java && java -cp /tmp/gson_classes:/tmp/repro Repro3"}", "name": "bash"}, "id": "call_-7355604559277847013", "index": 0, "type": "function"}]}}], "created": 1700000032, "id": "synthesized-00032", "model": "glm-5.2", "object": "chat.completion", "request_id": "synthesized-00032", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 0, "prompt_tokens": 0, "total_tokens": 0}}
